  "configuration_id": "config_017",
  "reason": "Evidence: All completed experiments use scgpt as the RNA encoder, so we have zero information about whether a simpler representation (pca_n2000) would perform comparably. The best rna_only result is config_002 (scgpt, multiprofile, avgpool) at 0.5305 acc / 0.5152 F1, and the best multimodal result (config_006, scgpt + imagenet_vit_l) is only ~1% higher at 0.5420, suggesting the RNA representation may be the dominant factor. Question: config_017 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_002—only the RNA encoder changes. This directly tests whether the learned scgpt representation is necessary or whether a linear 2000-dim projection suffices. Why best next: Resolving the RNA encoder question is the highest-leverage uncertainty because it affects every downstream decision (whether multimodal fusion is worthwhile, which encoder to pair with, and whether the pipeline can be simplified). If PCA matches scgpt, it invalidates the complexity of the current best configs and redirects the search; if it falls well short, it confirms scgpt's value and lets us focus remaining budget on fusion/aggregation/image-encoder choices with confidence in the RNA backbone."
}

